{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":19779,"duration_api_ms":19765,"ttft_ms":19777,"num_turns":1,"result":"Let me work through all 4 steps.\n\n**Step 1: Python `merge_sorted_lists`**\n\n```python\ndef merge_sorted_lists(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Merge two sorted lists into a single sorted list in O(n+m) time.\"\"\"\n    result = []\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):\n        if a[i] <= b[j]:\n            result.append(a[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            result.append(b[j])\n            j += 1\n    result.extend(a[i:])\n    result.extend(b[j:])\n    return result\n```\n\n**Step 2: Edge-case handling (empty inputs return the other directly, no copy)**\n\n```python\ndef merge_sorted_lists(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Merge two sorted lists into a single sorted list in O(n+m) time.\n\n    If either input is empty, the other list is returned directly (no copy).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not a:\n        return b\n    if not b:\n        return a\n    result = []\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):\n        if a[i] <= b[j]:\n            result.append(a[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            result.append(b[j])\n            j += 1\n    result.extend(a[i:])\n    result.extend(b[j:])\n    return result\n```\n\n**Step 3: pytest tests**\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\ndef test_both_empty():\n    assert merge_sorted_lists([], []) == []\n\ndef test_first_empty():\n    assert merge_sorted_lists([], [1, 2, 3]) == [1, 2, 3]\n\ndef test_second_empty():\n    assert merge_sorted_lists([1, 2, 3], []) == [1, 2, 3]\n\ndef test_interleaved_values():\n    assert merge_sorted_lists([1, 3, 5], [2, 4, 6]) == [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\n```\n\n**Step 4: Rust translation with tests**\n\n```rust\npub fn merge_sorted_lists<T: Ord + Clone>(a: &[T], b: &[T]) -> Vec<T> {\n    if b.is_empty() {\n        return a.to_vec();\n    }\n    if a.is_empty() {\n        return b.to_vec();\n    }\n    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(a.len() + b.len());\n    let mut i: usize = 0;\n    let mut j: usize = 0;\n    while i < a.len() && j < b.len() {\n        if a[i] <= b[j] {\n            result.push(a[i].clone());\n            i += 1;\n        } else {\n            result.push(b[j].clone());\n            j += 1;\n        }\n    }\n    result.extend(a[i..].iter().cloned());\n    result.extend(b[j..].iter().cloned());\n    result\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn test_both_empty() {\n        assert_eq!(merge_sorted_lists::<i32>(&[], &[]), vec![]);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn test_interleaved() {\n        assert_eq!(\n            merge_sorted_lists(&[1, 3, 5], &[2, 4, 6]),\n            vec![1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\n        );\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn test_first_empty() {\n        assert_eq!(\n            merge_sorted_lists::<i32>(&[], &[1, 2, 3]),\n            vec![1, 2, 3]\n        );\n    }\n}\n```\n\nOK_DONE","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6dc32bec-0f15-4364-ada7-0f02c37a12a7","total_cost_usd":0.05161500000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":5948,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":875,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"luce-dflash":{"inputTokens":5948,"outputTokens":875,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.05161500000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ac6f66cf-7a71-4fc4-b368-c907149e6dbf"}
